  "body": "## Problem\n\nAfter the solidcore update in PR #3802, the refusal of `twisted_flank_off.step` comes from the vertex check, not from the read. The new message does not name the face (#93) or the place of the fault. The app pin lost the assert that named the face.\n\nThe review of #3802 found that the location is still available: `record.rs:158-169` drops `worst_edge`.\n\n## Fix\n\n- Carry `worst_edge` into the refusal message, so that the user sees where the model is bad (the face, the edge, or the coordinates).\n- Restore an assert in the app pin that checks that the message names the location.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Follow-up from the review of PR #3802.\n",
